From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 11:09:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/71] fix(witness): pin liveness-map ordering and confirm
 absent before orphaning (gcp-g98)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`mol-witness-patrol.toml`'s `recover-orphaned-beads` step listed the bead
query before the session roster in prose, but the operative instruction said
only "build the liveness map ONCE per cycle (before the per-bead loop)".
That parenthetical pins the map relative to the loop, not relative to the
bead list, so an agent reading it as marching orders builds the map first —
the unsafe order. A polecat that spawns and is assigned work between the map
read and the bead read is missing from the map, resolves to `absent`, and
per the step's own classification table is treated as orphaned: the witness
reopens the source bead and `git worktree remove --force`s the worktree out
from under a live, working polecat. Observed live on the throwaway witness
patrol at 2026-07-31T14:4x — the map predated both `gastown__polecat-gc-iia3`
and `throwaway/gastown.furiosa`; that cycle escaped only because its bead
list happened to run before the assignment landed.

Two changes, both recipe text (this is a formula defect, not Go):

1. Ordering is now explicit and mandatory — capture the candidate bead list
   FIRST, build the liveness map SECOND — stated in Step 1 and restated at
   the numbered instruction that previously said only "before the per-bead
   loop". The superset invariant is spelled out (a session can appear between
   the reads, but one a bead already names cannot retroactively vanish from a
   later roster read) so a future editor does not re-invert it.
2. Because recovery is destructive, an `absent` classification now requires a
   targeted live re-query of that one identity before any action. The
   pre-existing MAP_COUNT==0 fail-safe (gc-3tn8g) only catches an EMPTY map;
   a merely STALE map is fully populated, passes that check, and fails
   silently on exactly the beads whose sessions are newest. A failed
   confirmation read yields `unconfirmed`, which classifies as not-orphaned
   and skips the bead — an unreadable roster is never proof of absence. This
   guard holds even if the ordering above regresses.

Validation: TOML parses (tomllib) and the step description round-trips;
the confirmation jq expression was exercised standalone against live/closed
session, configured-named-identity session bead, and unknown-assignee inputs,
returning active/closed/awake/absent respectively. Repo gates green on the
branch: go vet ./..., go build ./..., go test -race ./..., golangci-lint run
./... (0 issues), python3 validate_registry.py registry.toml, pytest tests/
(101 passed, 7 skipped).

Pre-existing: `gofumpt -l .` flags 12 files under slack-channel/ and
slack-full/ on the base branch (e82ecfb). None are touched by this diff and
they are out of scope for this bead.
---
 gastown/formulas/mol-witness-patrol.toml | 69 +++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 61 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gastown/formulas/mol-witness-patrol.toml b/gastown/formulas/mol-witness-patrol.toml
index 449fc94..81fada9 100644
--- a/gastown/formulas/mol-witness-patrol.toml
+++ b/gastown/formulas/mol-witness-patrol.toml
@@ -144,7 +144,17 @@ This happens when:
 
 **Step 1: Find orphaned beads via session-ID liveness.**
 
-List beads assigned to agents in YOUR rig:
+**Ordering is mandatory: capture the candidate bead list FIRST, build the
+liveness map SECOND.** Both reads are snapshots of a city that keeps moving,
+and only this order is safe. Sessions can appear between the two reads, but a
+session that a bead already names cannot retroactively vanish from a *later*
+roster read — so a map built after the bead list is a superset of every
+assignee that list can name. Build the map first and the window inverts: a
+polecat that spawns and gets assigned work in between is missing from the map,
+resolves to `absent`, and has its live worktree force-removed by Step 2. Do not
+reorder these two reads.
+
+List beads assigned to agents in YOUR rig (FIRST read):
 ```bash
 gc bd list --status=in_progress --json --limit=0
 gc bd list --status=open --json --limit=0
@@ -156,7 +166,8 @@ open/unassigned before witness observes it; that requires a separate
 worktree-salvage scan keyed by `metadata.work_dir`. Bound Gastown polecat
 assignees use the shape `<rig>/{{binding_prefix}}<polecat-suffix>`.
 
-Get the full session roster for liveness checks:
+Get the full session roster for liveness checks (SECOND read — only after the
+bead list above has been captured):
 ```bash
 gc session list --state=all --json
 gc bd list --type=session --label=gc:session --include-infra --include-gates --all --json --limit=0
@@ -171,8 +182,12 @@ a NEW session with a different ID — the old one never comes back.
 
 **Liveness check procedure:**
 
-1. Build the assignee→state liveness map ONCE per cycle (before the
-   per-bead loop), then resolve each bead's assignee against it. Resolve by
+1. Build the assignee→state liveness map ONCE per cycle (after the bead list
+   is captured, before the per-bead loop), then resolve each bead's assignee
+   against it. The map MUST be built after the bead-list snapshot so it stays a
+   superset of every assignee that list can name — that is the ordering mandate
+   in Step 1, and it is what keeps a session spawned mid-cycle from resolving to
+   `absent`. Do not re-invert it. Resolve by
    exact identifier lookup — do NOT extract a session ID with a regex or
    fixed prefix list: rig prefixes are configuration-derived, and assignees
    may be a session bead ID, session name, alias, concrete agent name, or
@@ -237,15 +252,53 @@ a NEW session with a different ID — the old one never comes back.
    pool/ephemeral work identities. If the assignee is a refinery, witness, or
    other configured infrastructure identity, skip it instead of recovering it.
 
-3. Classify:
+3. **Confirm every `absent` with a targeted live re-query before acting on
+   it.** Recovery is destructive — it force-removes a worktree and reopens the
+   source bead — so one stale map lookup must never be enough to trigger it.
+   The `MAP_COUNT==0` fail-safe above only catches an EMPTY map; a map that is
+   merely STALE is fully populated, passes that check, and fails silently on
+   exactly the beads whose sessions are newest. Re-read that ONE identity and
+   only keep `absent` if the second read agrees:
+   ```bash
+   if [ "$STATE" = "absent" ]; then
+     CONFIRM_SESSIONS=$(mktemp); CONFIRM_BEADS=$(mktemp)
+     if gc session list --state=all --json > "$CONFIRM_SESSIONS" \
+       && gc bd list --type=session --label=gc:session --include-infra --include-gates --all --json --limit=0 > "$CONFIRM_BEADS"; then
+       STATE=$(jq -r -n --arg a "$ASSIGNEE" \
+         --slurpfile sessions "$CONFIRM_SESSIONS" --slurpfile session_beads "$CONFIRM_BEADS" '
+         ([ ($sessions[0].sessions // [])[]
+            | select((.id == $a) or (.name == $a) or (.session_name == $a)
+                     or (.alias == $a) or (.agent_name == $a))
+            | (if (.closed // false) then "closed" else (.state // "") end) ]
+          + [ ($session_beads[0] // [])[]
+            | select(.metadata.configured_named_identity == $a)
+            | (if (.status == "closed") then "closed" else (.metadata.state // "") end) ])
+         | first // "absent"')
+     else
+       STATE="unconfirmed"
+     fi
+     rm -f "$CONFIRM_SESSIONS" "$CONFIRM_BEADS"
+   fi
+   ```
+   A confirmation read that FAILS (non-zero exit, empty file, unparseable JSON)
+   is NOT proof of absence — that is what `unconfirmed` means, and an
+   `unconfirmed` bead is skipped this cycle, not recovered. The re-read costs
+   one roster pair per absent candidate — rare in a healthy city — and it turns
+   an ordering race into a confirmed orphan. This is the guard that keeps
+   Step 2 safe even if the Step 1 ordering regresses.
+
+4. Classify:
    - `active` or `awake` → **not orphaned** (may be stuck —
      `check-polecat-health` handles that separately)
    - `creating`, `asleep`, `drained`, `suspended`, `draining`, or
      `quarantined` → **not orphaned** (controller or operator state still owns
      the session)
-   - `archived`, `closed`, or `absent` after the exact lookup → **orphaned
-     bead** for pool/ephemeral work — the owning session is gone and will never
-     come back, regardless of whether the pool template still exists
+   - `unconfirmed` (the item-3 re-query itself failed) → **not orphaned** —
+     skip the bead and let the next cycle re-evaluate it
+   - `archived`, `closed`, or an `absent` **confirmed by the item-3 re-query**
+     → **orphaned bead** for pool/ephemeral work — the owning session is gone
+     and will never come back, regardless of whether the pool template still
+     exists
 
 **Important**: Beads assigned to the refinery, witness, or other
 infrastructure agents (not pool instances) should be skipped — those
